I'm Olivier and I'm Mauritian. West of Mauritius is my guide to one stretch of coast. It starts at [Flic en Flac](/en/areas/flic-en-flac) in the north and ends at [Le Morne](/en/areas/le-morne) in the south with the hills of [Chamarel](/en/areas/chamarel) rising behind. I write it for people coming to visit and for people thinking of making a home here.

## What I try to do

I want every page to feel like advice from a friend who lives here. Where to swim when the wind picks up. Which village suits a young family. When to leave so you reach the viewpoint in the best light. And what buying a home really involves.

When something changes I update the page and the date shows it. If a place is featured or a link earns a commission you will see it marked. That never changes what I write.

## Where to start

- [The six areas](/en/areas) from Flic en Flac to Chamarel.
- [Guides](/en/guides) to the beaches and sunsets and hikes.
- [Living in the West](/en/living-in-the-west) if you are thinking of moving here.

## Get in touch

Spotted something out of date or know a place I should see? Write to me through the [contact page](/en/contact) or join the [west coast community](/en/community).
